.TH BASENAME 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
basename \- return non-directory portion of a pathname
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B basename
.I string
.RI [ suffix ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B basename
writes the final pathname component of
.I string
to standard output, followed by a newline.
.PP
If
.I suffix
is given, and it is not identical to the whole of the final pathname
component, and it is identical to a suffix of that component, the
.I suffix
is removed before the result is written.
.PP
Exactly one or two operands are accepted; no options are recognized.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I string
A pathname. An empty
.I string
produces a single
.BR . \|.
A
.I string
consisting entirely of one or more
.B /
characters (the root directory) produces a single
.BR / .
A drive-letter prefix such as
.B C:
is recognized and is never itself treated as the final pathname
component: a bare drive letter with no following separator (such as
.BR C: )
produces a single
.BR . \|,
and a drive root (such as
.BR C:\e )
produces the drive letter, colon, and one separator unchanged.
.TP
.I suffix
A suffix to remove from the final pathname component of
.IR string ,
if it is present there and is not the entire component.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
Writing the result to standard output failed.
.TP
.B 2
Fewer than one or more than two operands were given.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dirname (1),
.BR pathchk (1)
